# data-models-and-flow

### Invoice Queue Data Model

1. Core Queue Structure (Importance: 95)
- Stateful invoice queue with defined transitions:
  - NEW -> FOR_ME -> TO_BE_PAID -> COMPLETE
  - REJECTED state possible from any stage
- Each invoice contains:
  - Unique identifier
  - Current state
  - PDF location
  - Parsed data JSON
  - Approval metadata
  - QuickBooks sync status

2. Email Ingestion Flow (Importance: 85)
- Email attachment processing pipeline:
  - PDF extraction and deduplication
  - Vendor detection and routing
  - Parser selection and execution
  - Queue insertion with NEW status
- Maintains atomic operations with rollback capability

3. Approval Workflow (Importance: 90)
- Multi-stage approval process:
  - Initial categorization
  - Office assignment
  - Payment scheduling
  - QuickBooks bill creation
- Status transitions trigger specific actions:
  - FOR_ME -> Auto-categorization
  - TO_BE_PAID -> QuickBooks sync preparation
  - COMPLETE -> PDF attachment upload

4. QuickBooks Integration Flow (Importance: 85)
- Bidirectional sync process:
  - Queue monitors TO_BE_PAID invoices
  - Creates QuickBooks bills
  - Attaches original PDFs
  - Updates queue status
- Handles OAuth token management and renewal

5. State Persistence (Importance: 80)
- JSON-based queue storage:
  - Atomic write operations
  - Backup creation on updates
  - Version tracking
  - Recovery mechanisms
- Maintains invoice history and audit trail

